# ramtext.list - the hot functions lever L1 copies into RAM (S31GL_RAMTEXT=1;
# tinygl/source/s31_ramtext.c). One line per object: the source's basename,
# then its functions. A function takes its compiler clones with it
# (name.part.N, .isra.N, .constprop.N) and its .text.unlikely part.
#
# Chosen from the gl/bench per-function profile (prof.sh) of gears, glxgears,
# texobj and teapotf at 320x240 and 640x400 on the phase 4 tree: everything
# above ~0.5% of a frame on the per-vertex and per-triangle path, for the
# default depth test (GL_LESS with writes: ztriangle_lt.c). Left out, and
# why (artifacts/gl/phase4/REPORT.md, L1):
#   ZB_fill16            the clear: a 116-byte store loop, store-bound and
#                        resident in the I-cache wherever it lives
#   the clipper          gl_draw_triangle_clip, updateTmp, clip_*: ~1.5% of
#                        gears, 2 kB
#   the LEQUAL, no-depth and depth-mask fillers: none of the four demos uses
#                        them; the entry points exist (s31_rt), so adding a
#                        line here is all it takes
# Keep it small: the hart's I-cache is 16 KB (shared with the kernel), and
# the copy is RSS (whole pages) in every GL process that turns it on.
ztriangle_lt  ZB_fillTriangleFlat_lt ZB_fillTriangleSmooth_lt ZB_fillTriangleMappingPerspective_lt ztri_setup
vertex        gl_vertex4f
light         gl_shade_vertex
clip          gl_transform_to_viewport gl_draw_triangle gl_draw_triangle_fill gl_set_provoking_flat
list          glopCallList
# fill_pq_slow: reached from gl_draw_triangle_fill_pq by glxgears' smooth
# triangles every frame (review 4 R4-hot)
s31_tfilter   gl_draw_triangle_fill_pq fill_pq_slow
